## 5. MATHEMATICAL & CLINICAL ALGORITHMS

### 5.1 Mifflin-St Jeor Caloric & Macro Engine
Calculated in [[src/actions/profile.ts](file:///c:/Users/lenov/OneDrive/Desktop/HARSHIT/Projects/Agent%20Baymax/src/actions/profile.ts)]:

#### Step 1: Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR)
$$\text{BMR}_{\text{Male}} = 10 \times \text{weight (kg)} + 6.25 \times \text{height (cm)} - 5 \times \text{age (yrs)} + 5$$
$$\text{BMR}_{\text{Female}} = 10 \times \text{weight (kg)} + 6.25 \times \text{height (cm)} - 5 \times \text{age (yrs)} - 161$$
$$\text{BMR}_{\text{Other}} = \frac{\text{BMR}_{\text{Male}} + \text{BMR}_{\text{Female}}}{2}$$

#### Step 2: Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE)
$$\text{TDEE} = \text{BMR} \times \text{Activity Multiplier}$$
- Sedentary: $1.2$
- Lightly Active (1–3 days/week): $1.375$
- Moderately Active (3–5 days/week): $1.55$
- Very Active (6–7 days/week): $1.725$
- Extra Active (physical labor & training): $1.9$

#### Step 3: Caloric Adjustment by Goal
- **Lose Weight**:
  - Delta $< 5\text{ kg}$: $-350\text{ kcal}$
  - Delta $5\text{--}15\text{ kg}$: $-500\text{ kcal}$
  - Delta $> 15\text{ kg}$: $-600\text{ kcal}$
  - Obesity adjustment ($\text{BMI} > 30\text{ and Delta} > 15\text{ kg}$): Safe deficit of $-700\text{ kcal}$
  - Lean protection ($\text{BMI} < 22$): Deficit limited to maximum $-300\text{ kcal}$
  - Absolute medical minimum limit: $\max(\text{Calculated}, 1200\text{ kcal})$
- **Build Muscle**:
  - Delta $< 5\text{ kg}$: $+200\text{ kcal}$
  - Delta $\ge 5\text{ kg}$: $+350\text{ kcal}$
- **Maintain**: Exactly $0\text{ kcal}$ adjustment.

#### Step 4: Macronutrient Allocation
- **Protein**:
  - Lose Weight: $2.0\text{ g/kg}$ of body weight (preserves lean mass in deficit)
  - Build Muscle: $2.2\text{ g/kg}$ of body weight (supports muscular hypertrophy)
  - Maintain: $1.8\text{ g/kg}$ of body weight
- **Fat**:
  - Lose Weight: $20\%$ of target calories ($\text{Grams} = \frac{\text{Target Calories} \times 0.20}{9}$)
  - Build Muscle & Maintain: $25\%$ of target calories ($\text{Grams} = \frac{\text{Target Calories} \times 0.25}{9}$)
- **Carbohydrates**:
  - Fills the remaining caloric energy budget:
    $$\text{Carbs (g)} = \max\left(\frac{\text{Target Calories} - (\text{Protein g} \times 4) - (\text{Fat g} \times 9)}{4}, 50\text{ g}\right)$$

#### Step 5: Timeline Estimation
- Fat Loss: Rate of $0.5\text{--}1.0\text{ kg/week} \implies \text{Weeks} = \left[\frac{|\Delta|}{1.0}, \frac{|\Delta|}{0.5}\right]$
- Muscle Gain: Rate of $0.25\text{--}0.5\text{ kg/week} \implies \text{Weeks} = \left[\frac{\Delta}{0.5}, \frac{\Delta}{0.25}\right]$

---

### 5.2 Dynamic Hydration Target Formula
Calculated in [[src/components/features/water/HydrationDashboard.tsx](file:///c:/Users/lenov/OneDrive/Desktop/HARSHIT/Projects/Agent%20Baymax/src/components/features/water/HydrationDashboard.tsx)]:

$$\text{Daily Target (ml)} = \text{Baseline} + \text{Activity Increment} + \text{Goal Increment} + \text{Workout Recovery}$$
1. **Baseline**: $\text{Current Weight (kg)} \times 35\text{ ml/kg}$ (minimum default $2000\text{ ml}$).
2. **Activity Level Add-on**:
   - Sedentary: $+0\text{ ml}$
   - Lightly Active: $+350\text{ ml}$
   - Moderately Active: $+500\text{ ml}$
   - Very Active / Extra Active: $+750\text{ ml}$
3. **Goal Add-on**:
   - Lose Weight: $+250\text{ ml}$ (promotes satiety and metabolic clearance)
   - Build Muscle: $+500\text{ ml}$ (cellular hydration and protein synthesis)
   - Maintain: $+0\text{ ml}$
4. **Workout Recovery Toggle**: Toggling "Workout Day" adds $+800\text{ ml}$ for sweat and electrolyte balance recovery.
5. Final target rounded to the nearest $100\text{ ml}$.

