## 6. CORE SUBSYSTEMS & OPERATIONAL WORKFLOWS

### 6.1 Streaming Conversational AI & Asynchronous Long-Term Memory
- **Endpoint**: `/api/chat` (POST)
- **Model**: `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` via `streamText`
- **Flow**:
  1. Authenticates user session and token via Supabase SSR.
  2. Fetches user memories from `agent_memory` and formats them into the system prompt:
     ```
     IMPORTANT USER CONTEXT (Remember this):
     - [ALLERGIES] User is severely allergic to peanuts
     - [PREFERENCES] Prefers high-protein vegetarian meals
     ```
  3. Executes vector similarity search (`match_document_chunks`) on the latest user message to retrieve relevant clinical guide excerpts.
  4. If a meal photo URL is passed in the request body, executes vision analysis, commits the meal log, and passes the result into the chat prompt.
  5. Limits context window to the last 10 messages for token efficiency.
  6. Starts text streaming to the client.
  7. **Non-Blocking Callback (`onFinish`)**: Passes full history to [[extractAndStoreMemory](file:///c:/Users/lenov/OneDrive/Desktop/HARSHIT/Projects/Agent%20Baymax/src/lib/gemini/memory.ts)], which executes `generateObject` against `memoryExtractionSchema` and updates `agent_memory` (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE) without increasing stream latency.

