- **Modules**: [[src/proxy.ts](file:///c:/Users/lenov/OneDrive/Desktop/HARSHIT/Projects/Agent%20Baymax/src/proxy.ts)], [[src/lib/ratelimit.ts](file:///c:/Users/lenov/OneDrive/Desktop/HARSHIT/Projects/Agent%20Baymax/src/lib/ratelimit.ts)]
- **Flow**:
  1. Next.js proxy executes session updates via [[updateSession](file:///c:/Users/lenov/OneDrive/Desktop/HARSHIT/Projects/Agent%20Baymax/src/lib/supabase/middleware.ts)] to synchronize auth cookies across edge and server components.
  2. Route protection redirects unauthenticated requests for `/dashboard`, `/profile`, or `/chat` to `/login`.
  3. Requests to AI endpoints (`/api/chat`) evaluate client IP against an Upstash Redis sliding window limiter (10 requests per 10 seconds).
  4. Expensive actions (meal vision, knowledge ingestion) apply per-user limiters (5 requests per 60 seconds).
  5. **Fail-Open Design**: If Redis credentials are absent (local development) or Redis throws an error, the limiter fails open (`return true`) so valid user requests are never blocked.

